Z||000002||zeusrekning||12-05-2000||09:40 PM||||I'll make it related.<BR>I'd try to find a cheap fiero or by fiero parts if you allready have one.<BR>or you can donate it to the Carolina fiero association.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>i feel radar detectors are not a good investment unless you just have horrible luck and get pulled over often.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||12-05-2000||09:56 PM||||you want the top of the line?  best on the market?  then take my advice... <A HREF="http://www.k40.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.k40.com</A> <P>k 40 is the <B>best</B> detector manufactuar out there!  they don't advertise as much as the other guys, and they don't get tested in magazines, like the other guys.  <P>reason being, their main products are installed "hidden" units.  i installed one aa month after i bought my GT, and loved it.<P>these things work, and they stand behind their product!  <P>also, they used to recalibrate them for you (like a $50 charge), whenever you want.  i would send mine off ever couple of years and it came back with a different serial number on it... know what i mean?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  new receiver.<P>good luck!<P>hoop<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alien.gif">   <BR>We are not alone!||||reg||1
